THE HONEST-FAILURE CASE. `THERMAL_LIMITED` is deliberately NOT in the source
schema's mode enum — it stands for the mode a future producer adds, or a
typo, or a version skew between adapter and feed.

What this pins is that the mapping REFUSES rather than answers:

    power_state     POWER_STATE_UNSPECIFIED
    functional_mode FUNCTIONAL_MODE_UNSPECIFIED
    health_state    HEALTH_STATE_UNSPECIFIED
    actively_receiving / actively_transmitting   ABSENT

Before 2026-08-12 this input produced ON / ACTIVE / NOMINAL and both booleans
true — a fully healthy, actively-operating sensor, asserted on the strength
of not recognising its state. A safety-relevant false negative, and one that
propagated: ADR-0030 designates this file as the specimen adapter authors
copy, so the construction reproduced into every mapping written from it.

The catch-alls were not deleted; they were EMPTIED. Every mode the schema
declares is now listed explicitly and resolves exactly as it did before —
the other six cases in this suite are the proof of that, and their goldens
did not move when this fix landed. Only genuinely unrecognised input reaches
the final branch.

If someone later "simplifies" the match blocks back to a catch-all, the six
declared-mode cases will all still pass. This is the ONLY case that fails.
That is precisely why it exists.
